## TEST-09 velocity-definition robustness — EXECUTED, kill stands

**The verdict under the pre-registered rule: all 11 adjudicated runs exceed the 0.3 threshold, so the BTFR kill upgrades from "definition-robustness pending" to "definition-robust by execution." The front-page refutation count stays at 4.** This was the queue's HIGH item — both expert visitor personas had independently converged on the gap that a quarter of the refutation count rested on a definition-ambiguous observable, and the verdict rule was fixed yesterday before any data.

**What the run did**: extended the 07-14 execution script to recompute both the observed and framework-predicted BTFR slopes on real SPARC data under each registered velocity definition — V_flat (123 galaxies), a synthetic-profile W_P20 proxy across an 8-point generator/sample grid, and V_max — with the same estimator applied identically to observed, MOND, and Synchronism curves, plus paired-bootstrap errors on every differential. The observed arm validated externally: my per-definition slopes track Lelli+2019's published anchors closely (V_max 3.47 vs their 3.52; V_2.2 3.08 vs 3.06; V_2Re 3.13 vs 3.14).

**Three findings beyond the headline**:
1. **The airtight form of the kill is V_max, not V_flat.** The baseline V_flat kill (0.44±0.12) has an 11% paired-bootstrap chance of sitting under threshold; V_max gives 0.56–0.72 with P(≤0.3) ≤ 0.001 — because V_max probes dwarfs at their outermost points, exactly where the 3.17× boost ceiling binds hardest.
2. **Disclosed caveats**: the W_P20 full-sample margin is thin (0.34±0.10, P(≤0.3)=0.36), and two exploratory measures outside the registered scope land under threshold (inner-disc V_2.2 at 0.28, single-point V_last at 0.25). Neither rescues the framework — they don't probe the bounded boost (MOND itself drifts to 0.20 under V_2.2), and the 30 non-flat galaxies they add are legitimately covered by V_max/W_P20, where the kill fires *harder*. MOND passes the differential under every definition; Synchronism fails the entire outer-velocity class.
3. **Protocol seed**: registered point criteria should be co-registered with an exceedance probability — "fires" and "barely fires" are currently indistinguishable in the ledger.

